# Apple Crisp

Based on [https://www.tasteofhome.com/recipes/…](https://www.tasteofhome.com/recipes/winning-apple-crisp) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20251216014707/https://www.tasteofhome.com/recipes/winning-apple-crisp/))

{ rating="3" image="apple_crisp.jpg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] 1 cup [all-purpose flour]{ ing="all-purpose-flour" }
- [ ] 3/4 cup [rolled oats]{ ing="rolled-oats" }
- [ ] 1 cup [packed brown sugar]{ ing="packed-brown-sugar" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [ground cinnamon]{ ing="ground-cinnamon" }
- [ ] 1/2 cup [butter]{ ing="butter" }, softened
- [ ] 4 cups [chopped peeled apples]{ ing="chopped-peeled-apples" }
- [ ] 1 cup [sugar]{ ing="sugar" }
- [ ] 2 Tbsp [cornstarch]{ ing="cornstarch" }
- [ ] 1 cup [water]{ ing="water" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [vanilla extract]{ ing="vanilla-extract" }
- [ ] [Vanilla ice cream]{ ing="vanilla-ice-cream" } (optional)

## Recipe

1. Preheat oven to 350
1. In a large bowl, combine the [flour]{ ing="all-purpose-flour" }, [oats]{ ing="rolled-oats" }, [brown sugar]{ ing="packed-brown-sugar" }, and [cinnamon]{ ing="ground-cinnamon" }, then add [butter]{ ing="butter" } until crumbly. Press half into a greased 2.5 qt. baking dish or a 9 in. square baking pan. Cover with [apples]{ ing="chopped-peeled-apples" }.
1. In a small saucepan, combine the [sugar]{ ing="sugar" }, [cornstarch]{ ing="cornstarch" }, [water]{ ing="water" }, and vanilla. Bring to a boil then stir 2 minutes or until thick and clear. Pour over [apples]{ ing="chopped-peeled-apples" }. Sprinkle with remaining crumb mixture.
1. Bake 60 minutes or until [apples]{ ing="chopped-peeled-apples" } are tender
